title: The Halle Congress
subtitle: The USPD decides whether to join the International.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1920 and month = 10 and crisis = 0 and halle_done = 0 and ending_id = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
Q.halle_done = 1;
RG.news('Zinoviev in Halle: the USPD decides on Moscow', 3);
!}

= The Halle Congress

On 12 October the USPD congress opens in Halle. Four hundred delegates sit on two sides of the hall. Grigory Zinoviev has come from Moscow on a ten-day police permit. Julius Martov, the Menshevik, ill and hoarse, has come to warn the Germans what the Bolsheviks did to the Russian socialists.

On the 14th Zinoviev speaks in German for four hours, and Hilferding answers him for two. The vote is tomorrow. [? if twenty_one_conditions = 2 : The softened conditions have made it easier for the waverers. ?][? if twenty_one_conditions = 3 : The USPD right asks why it should accept conditions the communists themselves rejected. ?]

- @zinoviev: Leave it to Zinoviev.
- @promise: Promise the USPD's members an equal place in a united party.

@zinoviev
subtitle: Moscow's best speaker needs no help from us.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_halle_bonus = 1;
Q.independence -= 3;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 6);
!}
go-to: vote

@promise
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] No purge below the leaders. The waverers want to hear it.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.e20_halle_bonus = 2;
Q.uspd_relation += 5;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}
go-to: vote

@vote
title: The Vote
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
var score = Q.uspd_score + Q.e20_halle_bonus
    + (Q.twenty_one_conditions == 2 ? 2 : (Q.twenty_one_conditions == 3 ? -2 : 0))
    + (Q.uspd_relation >= 55 ? 1 : 0)
    + (Q.kapp_outcome == 3 ? -1 : 0)
    + Math.floor(Math.random() * 3);
if (score >= 9 && !Q.e20_attacked) {
    Q.uspd_split = 2;
    Q.uspd_relation += 15;
} else if (score >= 1) {
    Q.uspd_split = 1;
    Q.uspd_relation -= 10;
} else {
    Q.uspd_split = 3;
    Q.uspd_relation -= 15;
}
if (Q.kapp_outcome == 3 && Q.uspd_in_government && Q.uspd_split == 2) {
    Q.e20_uspd_ministers_left = 1;
    Q.uspd_in_government = 0;
    Q.government_name = 'Legien cabinet (SPD, unions)';
    Q.stability -= 5;
}
Q.e20_halle_won = (Q.uspd_split == 1 || Q.uspd_split == 2) ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.uspd_split == 3) { RG.news('Halle: the USPD rejects the conditions', 3); RG.ecci('zinoviev', -6); }
else { RG.news('Halle: the USPD votes to join the International', 3); RG.ecci('zinoviev', 8); RG.ledger('At Halle the USPD voted to join the International' + (Q.uspd_split == 2 ? ', almost whole.' : '.'), 'e20_halle'); }
RG.directiveUpdate();
!}

= The Vote

[? if uspd_split = 1 : On 16 October the congress votes 237 to 156 to accept the conditions. The minority walks out to hold its own congress in the same town. Crispien, Dittmann and Hilferding keep the name, the newspaper and most of the deputies. Däumig and Stoecker's majority prepares to unite with us. ?]

[? if uspd_split = 2 : The vote is overwhelming. Crispien and Dittmann give up the fight, and only Hilferding and a few dozen delegates walk out, most of them towards the SPD. The Independents, with their newspapers and their deputies, will unite with the communists. ?]

[? if uspd_split = 3 : The congress rejects the conditions, 214 to 179. Däumig and Stoecker lead the minority out of the hall. They are fewer than Moscow hoped. ?]

[? if e20_uspd_ministers_left = 1 : The USPD's ministers resign from Legien's cabinet the next day. Legien carries on with the SPD alone, at the mercy of the Centre. ?]
